  "issue_evidence": {
    "issue_number": 390,
    "repository": "scinfu/SwiftSoup",
    "title": "select() returns empty for attribute selector div[id='info-id'][data-type='info-data'] in v2.13.3 (works in v2.11.3)",
    "state": "closed",
    "issue_type": "bug_report_with_reproducer",
    "body": "I encountered a regression when upgrading from v2.11.3 to v2.13.3. The same CSS selector that successfully matches an element in v2.11.3 returns an empty result in v2.13.3.\n\n```swift\nlet html = \"...\"\nlet doc = try SwiftSoup.parse(html)\nlet el = try doc.select(\"div[id='info-id'][data-type='info-data']\")\n// empty in v2.13.3, non-empty in v2.11.3\n```\n\nThis is a compound attribute selector regression in the fast query path.",
    "fix_commit": "9bbf537ad234747bbf72730411c11b3fe5b1bc4e",
    "fix_message": "Fix compound attribute selector regression in fast query path"
  },
